Decode correctly and faster on subgroup-size-8 GPUs (Mali) — PUNKTFUNK LOCAL PATCH.

Upstream: Themaister/pyrowave #35 (open) carries the correctness fix.

WHY. Mali-G52 (LG webOS TVs) runs Vulkan with a fixed subgroup size of 8. wavelet_dequant.comp
assumed at least 16 lanes per subgroup, so on Mali it wrote wrong coefficients and the picture
was garbage. The shared-memory iDWT was also too slow there: the GPU is DRAM bandwidth bound
(about 1.9 GB/s of writes), so barriers and shared-memory round trips dominated.

WHAT IT DOES. Fixes the dequant for subgroups under 16, reads payload words instead of bytes,
and adds idwt_shuf.comp, an iDWT that does its horizontal lifting with subgroup shuffles across
the 8 lanes (no shared memory, no barriers). Selected only when the subgroup size is 8, so other
GPUs keep upstream's shaders. Includes the regenerated shaders/slangmosh.hpp. Measured on the
G52 (1080p, 1.66 MB frame): 28.7 -> 15.9 ms per decode.

